{
  "__inputs": [
    {
      "name": "DS_PROMETHEUS",
      "label": "Prometheus",
      "description": "",
      "type": "datasource",
      "pluginId": "prometheus",
      "pluginName": "Prometheus"
    }
  ],
  "__requires": [
    {
      "type": "grafana",
      "id": "grafana",
      "name": "Grafana",
      "version": "10.0.0"
    },
    {
      "type": "datasource",
      "id": "prometheus",
      "name": "Prometheus",
      "version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "type": "panel",
      "id": "timeseries",
      "name": "Time series",
      "version": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "panel",
      "id": "stat",
      "name": "Stat",
      "version": ""
    }
  ],
  "id": null,
  "uid": "sbproxy-mesh-storage",
  "title": "SBProxy Mesh Admission and Storage",
  "description": "Mesh inbound connection admission and the storage backend the mesh persists into. Both halves report only where the mesh runs with its Redis backend, so read the Mesh Node Isolation and Storage Backend Reporting tiles before reading any empty chart here as health.",
  "tags": [
    "sbproxy",
    "mesh",
    "storage"
  ],
  "style": "dark",
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "refresh": "10s",
  "version": 1,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Mesh Node Isolation",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "text": "Mesh up, not isolated",
                  "color": "green",
                  "index": 0
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "Split-brain quarantine",
                  "color": "red",
                  "index": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "noValue": "Mesh not enabled"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(mesh_node_isolated)",
          "legendFormat": "isolated",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Whether any scraped node is in split-brain quarantine, and, by being present at all, whether the mesh is running. Mesh bootstrap publishes this gauge at 0 the moment it builds its isolation observer, so No data means no scraped process runs the mesh and every mesh panel below is empty for that reason rather than because admission is healthy. Read this tile before reading any of them. A 1 means at least one node saw fewer alive peers than its configured minimum and quarantined itself; fix the partition, or lower the mesh minimum if the cluster legitimately shrank, before reading anything into the rejection counters below."
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Inbound Rejections, Last 5m",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 10
              }
            ]
          },
          "noValue": "None recorded"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(increase(mesh_transport_inbound_rejected_total{reason!=\"idle_timeout\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "rejections",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Inbound mesh RPC connections this node refused or tore down in the last five minutes, counting only the five reasons that are a fault. The idle_timeout reason is excluded because the client half recycles a connection only when it next sends, so a quiet cluster reclaims idle peer connections routinely and would hold this tile yellow forever. Any sustained value means peers are being turned away: read the reason breakdown below for which control fired, then the mesh transport log for the peer address, which is deliberately not a metric label."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Storage Op Errors, Last 5m",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 25
              }
            ]
          },
          "noValue": "None recorded"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(increase(sbproxy_storage_op_errors_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "errors",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Storage backend operations that returned an error in the last five minutes, across every operation, backend, and record kind. Nonzero means the mesh's shared store is failing work. Split it on the error-kind panel below before acting: disconnected and timeout are the backend or the network, key_too_large and value_too_large are a caller writing oversize records and will not clear on their own."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Storage Backend Reporting",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "1": {
                  "text": "Not in use",
                  "color": "text",
                  "index": 0
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "noValue": "Reporting"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "absent(sbproxy_storage_op_duration_seconds_count)",
          "legendFormat": "absent",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Whether any storage operation has been observed at all. absent() returns 1 when no scraped process has recorded a single storage call, which is the normal state for a deployment that does not run the mesh with its Redis backend, because that backend is the only production caller of the storage layer today. When this reads Not in use, treat the four storage panels below as unconfigured rather than as healthy. No action unless you expected that backend to be running."
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Mesh Inbound Rejections by Reason",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "pointSize": 5,
            "showPoints": "auto"
          },
          "noValue": "No rejections recorded. Check the Mesh Node Isolation tile before reading this as healthy: it is also what a deployment with no mesh looks like."
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "connection_limit"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "fixedColor": "red",
                  "mode": "fixed"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "handshake_failed"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "fixedColor": "orange",
                  "mode": "fixed"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "idle_timeout"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "fixedColor": "text",
                  "mode": "fixed"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (rate(mesh_transport_inbound_rejected_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{reason}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Every admission and deadline control on the inbound half of the mesh transport, split by which one fired. connection_limit means the node hit its inbound connection cap and closed the peer without spawning a task, so raise the cap or shrink the peer set. handshake_timeout and handshake_failed are mesh mTLS: a missing client certificate, one the mesh CA did not sign, or a handshake that ran past its deadline. frame_timeout and write_timeout are a peer that opened a request and then stopped sending or stopped reading. idle_timeout is charted here for completeness and is not a fault; a quiet cluster moves that line on its own, which is why the alert rule excludes it. The peer address is in the transport log line, never in a label."
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Mesh Admission Failures by Operator Fix",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 5
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "pointSize": 5,
            "showPoints": "auto"
          },
          "noValue": "No rejections recorded. Check the Mesh Node Isolation tile before reading this as healthy: it is also what a deployment with no mesh looks like."
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Capacity: inbound connection cap"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "fixedColor": "red",
                  "mode": "fixed"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Identity: mesh mTLS"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "fixedColor": "orange",
                  "mode": "fixed"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Peer stalled mid-request"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "fixedColor": "yellow",
                  "mode": "fixed"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Idle reclaim, not a fault"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "fixedColor": "text",
                  "mode": "fixed"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(mesh_transport_inbound_rejected_total{reason=\"connection_limit\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "Capacity: inbound connection cap",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum(rate(mesh_transport_inbound_rejected_total{reason=~\"handshake_timeout|handshake_failed\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "Identity: mesh mTLS",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "sum(rate(mesh_transport_inbound_rejected_total{reason=~\"frame_timeout|write_timeout\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "Peer stalled mid-request",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "expr": "sum(rate(mesh_transport_inbound_rejected_total{reason=\"idle_timeout\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "Idle reclaim, not a fault",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "The same counter as the panel beside it, regrouped so each line maps to one thing an operator can change. Capacity means raise this node's inbound connection cap or shrink the peer set. Identity means fix the mesh CA trust or the peer's client certificate. Peer stalled means look at the peer rather than at this node: it opened a request and then stopped talking. Idle reclaim is drawn deliberately and is normal housekeeping, so do not treat a moving grey line as an incident; the alert rule leaves it out for that reason."
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "title": "Storage Operation Latency",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "pointSize": 5,
            "showPoints": "auto"
          },
          "noValue": "No storage traffic recorded. The mesh Redis backend is the only caller of the storage layer today, so this is what a deployment without it looks like, not a fast one."
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "p99"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "fixedColor": "red",
                  "mode": "fixed"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le) (rate(sbproxy_storage_op_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(sbproxy_storage_op_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(sbproxy_storage_op_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Round-trip latency of storage backend calls, across every operation. The histogram's last real bucket is 1 second, so a p99 pinned at the top of the chart means calls are landing in the overflow bucket and the true number is worse than the line shows. Sustained p99 above a few tens of milliseconds against a same-zone Redis is a backend or network problem rather than a caller one; take it to the per-operation panel beside this before changing mesh settings."
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Storage p99 Latency by Operation",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 13
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "pointSize": 5,
            "showPoints": "auto"
          },
          "noValue": "No storage traffic recorded. The mesh Redis backend is the only caller of the storage layer today, so this is what a deployment without it looks like, not a fast one."
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le, op) (rate(sbproxy_storage_op_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{op}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "The same p99, split by the operation the caller issued. The scanning operations, list_prefix and smembers, are expected to sit above the single-key ones; that is not a regression by itself. A get or a put drifting up alongside them points at the backend, while one operation moving alone points at the call site that issues it. Use this to decide which of the two to open."
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "title": "Storage Errors by Error Kind",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 21
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "pointSize": 5,
            "showPoints": "auto"
          },
          "noValue": "No storage traffic recorded. The mesh Redis backend is the only caller of the storage layer today, so this is what a deployment without it looks like, not a fast one."
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "disconnected"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "fixedColor": "red",
                  "mode": "fixed"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "timeout"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "fixedColor": "orange",
                  "mode": "fixed"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (error_kind) (rate(sbproxy_storage_op_errors_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{error_kind}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Storage failures split by the error variant the backend returned. disconnected means the store is unreachable and the mesh has lost its shared state; check Redis and the network path first. timeout means it answered too slowly to be useful. key_too_large and value_too_large are a caller writing past the storage layer's key and value caps, and they repeat until that call site is fixed. invalid_config is a store built with settings it rejects. backend is everything Redis itself reported as an error."
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "title": "Storage Errors by Operation and Record Kind",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 21
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "pointSize": 5,
            "showPoints": "auto"
          },
          "noValue": "No storage traffic recorded. The mesh Redis backend is the only caller of the storage layer today, so this is what a deployment without it looks like, not a fast one."
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (op, kind) (rate(sbproxy_storage_op_errors_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{op}} / {{kind}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "The same failures, split by which call and which record shape produced them. One operation carrying all of the error rate points at a single call site or a single Redis data structure. Errors spread evenly across every operation point at the connection instead. Read this before the error-kind panel decides your next step, because backend covers both cases."
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "title": "Storage Operation Rate by Operation",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 29
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
