      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (op) (rate(sbproxy_storage_op_duration_seconds_count[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{op}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Throughput of the storage layer, taken from the latency histogram's count series because there is no separate operation counter. This is the denominator for the error ratio beside it, and it is also how you tell a quiet mesh from a stalled one: a running mesh issues membership and persistence calls every maintenance round, so a flat zero here while the Mesh Node Isolation tile reports means the maintenance loop is not running and wants a process restart or a log read."
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "title": "Storage Error Ratio",
