      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(sbproxy_storage_op_errors_total[5m])) / sum(rate(sbproxy_storage_op_duration_seconds_count[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "Errors / operations",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Failed storage operations as a fraction of all of them. The latency histogram is observed on success and on failure alike, so the denominator contains the numerator and this really is bounded to 0 and 1. Anything sustained above one percent is worth a ticket. Anything near 1 means the store is effectively down and the mesh is running without shared state, which is the SBPROXY-STORAGE-BACKEND-ERRORS condition. Returns nothing rather than zero when there is no storage traffic to divide."
    },
