        }
      ],
      "description": "What the optional NATS and ClickHouse request-event sinks did with each event. published is a batch the destination confirmed: for NATS that is a PONG after the publishes, for ClickHouse a 2xx on the insert. dropped is the hand-off queue at capacity, which means the request path outran the sink and events were discarded rather than made to wait on a broker. error is a batch the destination did not take, and it is lost: this sink does not retry, because holding a request-event batch is a spool with its own operational surface. reconnected counts broker redials, and a steady rate there is a broker cycling rather than a healthy one."
